$ Tiny non-square kakuro for testing.
$ kakuro.eprime declares `find grid : matrix indexed by [X,Y]` with X = 1..width and
$ Y = 1..height — first index is the row axis and second is the column axis, so the
$ visible grid is 2 rows × 3 cols.  Regression target: rendering must derive
$ puzzle.width=3 / puzzle.height=2 from the matrix shape, not the param names.

letting width be 2
letting height be 3

letting blanks be
[
    [0,0,0],
    [0,1,1]
]

letting vertsums be
[
    [0,1,2],
    [0,0,0]
]

letting horzsums be
[
    [0,0,0],
    [3,0,0]
]
